;; and java-diagnostics', the union of their levels' kept ids), the rest a seventh a night. Written by bin/gate-subsets java
;; (test/gate/subsets.ae's rule, checked by bin/gate-subsets java --check): of the corpus's JDK passes, the controls' subjects,
;; the tests a class of test/java/divergences.edn at the level names (:tests, :examples), those that ever failed in the rotation
;; (test/gate/failed-ever.tsv) and one per class held by :match alone, then each area (the :areas prefix plus :dir's next
;; component) filled to a fifth in ascending SHA-256 of the id. java-check itself does not read them.
;; :night (JCS337 (a), the user 2026-11-09): the corpora's night. A corpus with :night N is in the scan once the file's
;; :night is N or more (java.check/active-corpora; JAVA_CHECK_NIGHT overrides it by hand, for a sample whose reference
;; lines are not committed): the night that records corpus N raises :night to N (test/java/night-corpora.bash N) and
